{"agent":"bg107","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_run_locked` and `_run_under_slot` now unpack three values from `_execute` (`p, out_prefix, elapsed = _execute(...)`), and the new docstring says the third is elapsed seconds summed across stages, but the only body change is `spent = p.elapsed_s` before the selected-scope stage. That name is never added to, never returned, and the following hunk ends at `scope.unran = unran`, so the real return is still the old 2-tuple. A normal `ddflow ci run` (full suite or selected) therefore raises `ValueError: not enough values to unpack` before `_settled_result` can set `elapsed_s`, so timed outcomes are not recorded at all. Even if a later return used `spent`, it is snapshotted on the pre-selection process only, so a selected run's second stage would not be included in the sum the comment claims.","digest":"e17d2f643f4dccc8","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:552","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:552"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21508,"diff_sha":"4c84cf70795453f0bba84aebb12601f6ec7c75d9c9169e8d04fef3e816d9eec3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B28537b615d","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":85.7,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"df43ed409f6d3bf8","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B28537b615d.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261109T021206Z-172a9bd8.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"b53d506326b83efac844f8f07ea19aad61d0b567","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/cirun.py":"100644 0d8cfde69435f2d4a293c9a9bd8606bf5c1e7185","ddflow/api/gates/_vet.py":"100644 69034b95534e8ceac3c2915d7f174b4173bb6e1e","ddflow/services/ci/runner.py":"100644 a5f193c4d2607e5962542fc08dbe91df91113e22"