{"agent":"bg107","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_run_locked` and `_run_under_slot` now unpack `_execute(...)` as three values (`p, out_prefix, elapsed`), but the only edit inside `_execute` is `spent = p.elapsed_s` and that name is never returned. On any real run the call raises `ValueError: not enough values to unpack (expected 3, got 2)` before `_settled_result` can set `elapsed_s`, so timed outcomes are still not recorded.","digest":"4619ec2d3c6c0795","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_execute","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_execute"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The early return now passes `spent`, but the only assignment of `spent` (`before, spent = p.output, p.elapsed_s`) was removed and the remaining `before = p.output` sits after that return. On any run that does not both select a command and exit 0 — the failed-full, failed-selected, and partial cases this bug says are untimed — that path raises `NameError` before a verdict can be recorded, so `ddflow ci run` crashes instead of attaching `elapsed_s`. The later `return p, before, spent` has the same hole unless some unshown line rebinds `spent`.","digest":"46a21ee5c3644eac","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:562","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:562"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21508,"diff_sha":"4c84cf70795453f0bba84aebb12601f6ec7c75d9c9169e8d04fef3e816d9eec3","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B28537b615d","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":49.1,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"6c644611eadad4c1","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B28537b615d.critic.grok-4.7.20261109T021448Z-59e49f24.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"f